Clover's optional exact suffix lookup drafter adapts the bounded prompt/history
lookup in VecSzn/PolyStrata, include/strata/spec/suffix_drafter.hpp and
src/spec/suffix_drafter.cpp at a82999fd60c2b6b3dbfb3924df60f8ff756c4371
(MIT). It proposes existing token continuations; TinyStrata verifies them with
the full causal model and preserves response-only generation penalties.
The optional Qwen/Gemma suffix proposal paths reuse that bounded lookup. Their
measured proposal-depth and lookup gating policies also consult PolyStrata's
Guesses/DraftPolicy cost and probe design at the same commit (MIT). TinyStrata
retains full target-model sampling and computes every selected Expert; proposal
scheduling does not introduce approximate acceptance or Expert omission.

Qwen3.6 native-server consumed-history tracking follows Strata Flash-Next's
src/program/generate.cpp at the base commit listed above (MIT), recording the
whole committed speculative prefix before emitting a potentially shorter reply.

